/**
 * Models BioNetGen will not produce a network for, with the reason measured per
 * class rather than asserted.
 *
 * A reference must be exactly what BioNetGen produces for a model *as published*.
 * The pipeline used to inject `*__FREE` defaults and append
 * `generate_network`/`simulate`, manufacturing references for models BioNetGen
 * rejects — so the gate was comparing our run of one model against a reference for
 * a modified one. That injection is gone, and the cost is that these models now
 * have no reference at all. They must therefore be declared here, or the
 * network-shape gate fails on them.
 *
 * Every reason below was measured by running BioNetGen on the published source
 * and reading its abort, against akutuva21/bionetgen at 3513bca7. Models that
 * aborted only because NFsim was absent from the auditing environment are
 * deliberately NOT listed: CI installs NFsim, so declaring them would hide a real
 * difference.
 *
 * Keys are lowercased basenames.
 */
